      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sure, let's break it down. First, subtract the salvage value from the cost of the CNC milling machine, that’s $85,000 - $5,000 = $80,000. Then, divide that result by the estimated useful life; $80,000 ÷ 7 years = $11,428.57 per year. The straight-line depreciation expense for the first year would be $11,428.57.",
